WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.482
- Good morning Believe Nation!

00:00:01.482 --> 00:00:04.370
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.526
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to

00:00:06.526 --> 00:00:09.704
solve all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.704 --> 00:00:11.046
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:15.199
we're going to learn how success
is the hangover of failure.

00:00:15.199 --> 00:00:16.907
Over to you, Marc Ecko.

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:19.066
(rooster crowing)

00:00:19.066 --> 00:00:21.399
(rap music)

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:32.436
- I think the best advice
that I could give you

00:00:33.445 --> 00:00:37.067
on success is to know that success

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.002
is merely the hangover of failure.

00:00:40.002 --> 00:00:44.152
And that failure is an
essential ingredient

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:46.959
in creating a learning atmosphere for you.

00:00:46.959 --> 00:00:49.565
So that you can accrue those learnings,

00:00:49.565 --> 00:00:53.311
those small, incremental, steps of failure

00:00:53.311 --> 00:00:54.982
and collect enough learning so

00:00:54.982 --> 00:00:57.834
that you can arrive at success, right?

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:01.586
I think that we're taught in the system

00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:03.461
that failure is something that

00:01:03.461 --> 00:01:05.583
you should be ashamed of.

00:01:05.583 --> 00:01:08.439
Failure is for the dumb kids

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:11.047
cause you get an F, you get a D, right?

00:01:11.047 --> 00:01:13.285
You're not competent, you didn't comply.

00:01:13.285 --> 00:01:16.337
You didn't create the
evidence of your worthiness.

00:01:16.337 --> 00:01:19.149
And I could tell you, as
someone who's successful,

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:21.474
right, both financially, from a

00:01:21.474 --> 00:01:22.697
wealth creation point of view,

00:01:22.697 --> 00:01:24.731
but more importantly
a wealth that matters,

00:01:24.731 --> 00:01:27.987
that success doesn't look like an A+.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.043
It doesn't look like 110 in extra credit.

00:01:31.043 --> 00:01:34.829
And failure isn't as simple as an F.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:39.189
And it's not always, like,
failure can be very gray, right?

00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:42.898
And being able to discern
what you might arrive at

00:01:42.898 --> 00:01:46.527
an event in your life
where you think that,

00:01:46.527 --> 00:01:48.156
"Wow, I've succeeded."

00:01:48.156 --> 00:01:50.031
And you're getting the affirmation

00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:52.273
from all these outside forces.

00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:54.350
But if it's not aligned authentically

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.815
to who and what you are,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.843
it could very much feel like failure.

00:01:57.843 --> 00:01:59.146
- Failure is only real failure

00:01:59.146 --> 00:02:00.529
if you don't learn anything from it.

00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:02.732
We're so caught up on failure as

00:02:02.732 --> 00:02:04.972
being this really bad, negative thing,

00:02:04.972 --> 00:02:08.026
and what happens is people take one shot,

00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:11.275
and if they don't hit, then they quit.

00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:15.232
In what world do you take
one shot, and make it?

00:02:15.232 --> 00:02:16.900
It's very rare.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.669
It takes a shot, after another
shot, after another shot

00:02:19.669 --> 00:02:23.455
in business, in life,
in athletics, in music,

00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:25.738
anything that you want to do.

00:02:25.738 --> 00:02:28.309
You will suck at the beginning.

00:02:28.309 --> 00:02:31.812
You will fail over and over
and over and over again.

00:02:31.812 --> 00:02:34.503
And because people don't
hit it on their first try,

00:02:34.503 --> 00:02:37.268
they're convinced that it's
never going to work out for them.

00:02:37.268 --> 00:02:39.265
And quite often, then they become

00:02:39.265 --> 00:02:40.935
the little man to other people and say,

00:02:40.935 --> 00:02:42.442
"Because I didn't achieve my goal,

00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:44.477
now you can't go out and
achieve yours either."

00:02:44.477 --> 00:02:46.514
It's never going to work
and they become this

00:02:46.514 --> 00:02:49.038
super negative person who
just brings everybody down.

00:02:49.038 --> 00:02:52.290
Most people are so afraid to
fail that they don't even try.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.897
And that's the biggest failure of all.

00:02:54.897 --> 00:02:57.910
Understand that it only
takes one thing to hit

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.808
for you to become a massive success.

00:03:00.808 --> 00:03:02.601
If you look at actors, a lot of people had

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:06.105
a tiny role, after a tiny
role, after a tiny role

00:03:06.105 --> 00:03:07.817
and they look back on their roles now

00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:09.976
and they cringe on their acting abilities.

00:03:09.976 --> 00:03:11.399
But that's how they got started.

00:03:11.399 --> 00:03:12.664
And none of those were hits

00:03:12.664 --> 00:03:14.659
and eventually they had
their big break through.

00:03:14.659 --> 00:03:16.491
You look at entrepreneurs,
it's the same thing.

00:03:16.491 --> 00:03:18.564
A lot of entrepreneurs start
with a little business,

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.049
and a little business and
another one that doesn't go well.

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:22.513
And it under, and a little business.

00:03:22.513 --> 00:03:24.223
And then they come up
with that idea that really

00:03:24.223 --> 00:03:26.708
takes off and they make their
first successful company.

00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:28.664
If we look at my YouTube
channel as an example,

00:03:28.664 --> 00:03:30.218
I've done so many videos.

00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:32.705
4,000 videos on the channel.

00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:35.594
And it took a long time
before any of them hit.

00:03:35.594 --> 00:03:37.911
If you look at the Top
Ten series, as an example,

00:03:37.911 --> 00:03:40.481
I tried that as one idea.

00:03:40.481 --> 00:03:42.726
And that was one out of tons of ideas.

00:03:42.726 --> 00:03:44.314
And that idea hit.

00:03:44.314 --> 00:03:46.145
And then that became from once a week,

00:03:46.145 --> 00:03:47.920
to twice a week to five times a week.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.609
And thanks to your feedback,

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:52.863
we're able to collect 3,000 plus votes

00:03:52.863 --> 00:03:56.384
on different people to profile
because I never thought

00:03:56.384 --> 00:03:58.700
that we'd have enough people to profile

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.446
52 in a year.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:02.068
I thought that was maximum.

00:04:02.068 --> 00:04:03.663
Double that, 100 in a year,

00:04:03.663 --> 00:04:05.335
let alone five times a week.

00:04:05.335 --> 00:04:07.003
I didn't think we had enough content.

00:04:07.003 --> 00:04:09.086
And you guys provided it to me.

00:04:09.086 --> 00:04:12.139
We have cut more series on this channel

00:04:12.139 --> 00:04:13.975
than most people create.

00:04:13.975 --> 00:04:14.992
I'm okay with cutting.

00:04:14.992 --> 00:04:17.519
I get an idea, the first
thing I want to do,

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:18.661
and here's the process,

00:04:18.661 --> 00:04:19.842
the first thing I do when I get

00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:21.677
an idea is I want to try it.

00:04:21.677 --> 00:04:22.696
Test it.

00:04:22.696 --> 00:04:24.571
Don't make it some big, crazy thing

00:04:24.571 --> 00:04:26.646
that becomes impossible to ever do.

00:04:26.646 --> 00:04:29.130
If you get an idea, find a low cost,

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:33.252
low, super easy way to
get started on trying it.

00:04:33.252 --> 00:04:35.580
And see, do you like it?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.252
Does it make you come alive?

00:04:37.252 --> 00:04:38.431
Do you want to go do it again?

00:04:38.431 --> 00:04:39.979
Was there any kind of reaction to it?

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.403
How can you make it better and tweak it?

00:04:41.403 --> 00:04:45.350
Or, it was not enjoyable.
I don't like doing that.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.695
I don't want to do it anymore.

00:04:46.695 --> 00:04:47.915
People didn't like it either.

00:04:47.915 --> 00:04:49.097
So we're going to cut.

00:04:49.097 --> 00:04:51.170
Success will come again when you combine

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.937
the thing that you love doing
with what the market wants.

00:04:53.937 --> 00:04:55.647
The thing that you
absolutely have a passion for

00:04:55.647 --> 00:04:56.869
with what people want.

00:04:56.869 --> 00:04:58.331
You have to have both.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.007
If it's just what you want,

00:05:00.007 --> 00:05:02.040
then it's just a hobby
that you do for yourself.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.055
If it's just what the market
wants, consumers want,

00:05:05.055 --> 00:05:06.442
then you're never going to be the best

00:05:06.442 --> 00:05:07.744
because you're only doing it for money

00:05:07.744 --> 00:05:09.008
and you don't have a passion to

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.231
really be great at that business.

00:05:10.231 --> 00:05:11.696
Has to be the combination.

00:05:11.696 --> 00:05:14.137
What you love doing,
with what people want.

00:05:14.137 --> 00:05:15.159
And if you love doing it,

00:05:15.159 --> 00:05:17.525
you haven't figured out
what people want yet,

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:19.117
then keep hustling, hustling, hustling

00:05:19.117 --> 00:05:21.194
until you can find value to those people

00:05:21.194 --> 00:05:23.064
so you can build a great business.

00:05:23.064 --> 00:05:24.692
But the next time you get this great idea,

00:05:24.692 --> 00:05:26.080
something that you want to do,

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.461
stop just making a list of different ideas

00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:32.351
that just, we keep adding
to our list of to-do's

00:05:32.351 --> 00:05:35.407
a list of ideas that one day
we want to do something about.

00:05:35.407 --> 00:05:38.179
Get over the fear of failure.

00:05:38.179 --> 00:05:39.854
Start small.

00:05:39.854 --> 00:05:42.870
Take that idea and find a way, today

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.830
to move forward on it and see,

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.500
does it make you come alive so you

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.555
want to keep doing it
again and again and again

00:05:49.555 --> 00:05:52.765
and if not, throw it away
and move on to the next one.

00:05:52.765 --> 00:05:54.676
Failure is only feedback.

00:05:54.676 --> 00:05:56.668
Failure is only showing you a way

00:05:56.668 --> 00:05:58.003
of how not to do something.

00:05:58.003 --> 00:06:00.401
And if you have that deep passion
for learning how to do it,

00:06:00.401 --> 00:06:03.900
don't quit on your dreams
because you're afraid of failing.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.204
So the question of the day today is:

00:06:05.204 --> 00:06:07.264
I'm curious, what is one
of the biggest lessons

00:06:07.264 --> 00:06:11.048
that you've learned from
failure in the past?

00:06:11.048 --> 00:06:12.432
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:06:12.432 --> 00:06:13.656
really curious to find out.

00:06:13.656 --> 00:06:14.959
I just want to give a quick shoutout to

00:06:14.959 --> 00:06:17.650
Michelle Bridgman from
michellebridgman.com.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.399
Michelle, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:19.399 --> 00:06:20.899
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:06:20.899 --> 00:06:22.893
It really, really means a lot to me

00:06:22.893 --> 00:06:24.079
and I hope you're enjoying reading it.

00:06:24.079 --> 00:06:25.300
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.642
I believe in you,

00:06:26.642 --> 00:06:28.682
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:28.682 --> 00:06:30.966
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:30.966 --> 00:06:32.794
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:32.794 --> 00:06:35.211
for another shot of espresso.

00:06:36.134 --> 00:06:38.467
(rap music)

00:06:44.662 --> 00:06:46.982
- You eventually joined
Harper's Bizarre US.

00:06:46.982 --> 00:06:49.982
And in 1976, it was, you were fired?

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:53.093
And I find that extraordinary.

00:06:53.093 --> 00:06:56.391
- No, they were very
clear in that they thought

00:06:56.391 --> 00:06:59.572
that I would never understand
the American market.

00:06:59.572 --> 00:07:03.739
I remember I was the editor
on one shoot that was,

00:07:05.441 --> 00:07:08.378
I think it was a French fashion show.

00:07:08.378 --> 00:07:12.978
And I decided that it would
be interesting to have

00:07:12.978 --> 00:07:14.689
dreadlocks on the models.

00:07:14.689 --> 00:07:16.884
And I think that that pushed them further

00:07:16.884 --> 00:07:18.634
than they could bear.

00:07:20.719 --> 00:07:22.748
So that was it for me.

00:07:22.748 --> 00:07:25.748
But I think it's always part of life

00:07:27.885 --> 00:07:30.572
to have some knocks as
well as some successes.

00:07:30.572 --> 00:07:31.796
- And to take risks?

00:07:31.796 --> 00:07:33.046
- And to learn.

00:07:33.911 --> 00:07:36.275
So I think it's healthy for everyone

00:07:36.275 --> 00:07:39.333
to lose a job as well as to gain a job.

00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:42.349
- You wake up in the
morning, you're failing.

00:07:42.349 --> 00:07:44.221
So you blame the President,
you blame Congress,

00:07:44.221 --> 00:07:46.788
you blame Greece, blame the Euro.

00:07:46.788 --> 00:07:48.745
I mean, construction industry,

00:07:48.745 --> 00:07:50.374
it's the mayor, oh, it's this.

00:07:50.374 --> 00:07:53.061
And you wake up in the morning
and you look in the mirror,

00:07:53.061 --> 00:07:55.667
and you're not failing because
it's the other guy's fault.

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:57.295
Or it's the economy's fault.

00:07:57.295 --> 00:07:59.083
But if you look in the mirror and said,

00:07:59.083 --> 00:08:02.012
I'm failing because of
me, you wouldn't like it.

00:08:02.012 --> 00:08:03.558
And you'd change that.

00:08:03.558 --> 00:08:05.512
And I believe the common denominator

00:08:05.512 --> 00:08:08.405
of failure in any business is excuses.

00:08:08.405 --> 00:08:11.374
As long as you wake up
and blame poor sales

00:08:11.374 --> 00:08:13.285
on the economy, or an environment,

00:08:13.285 --> 00:08:16.378
then you have no motivation
to make it better.

00:08:16.378 --> 00:08:17.847
Because it's not your fault.

00:08:17.847 --> 00:08:20.574
But in the worst economic environment,

00:08:20.574 --> 00:08:22.650
four or five years in this country ago,

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:25.445
the we've seen in our lifetimes,

00:08:25.445 --> 00:08:27.605
there were people making a
lot of money weren't there?

00:08:27.605 --> 00:08:28.986
In the height of that recession,

00:08:28.986 --> 00:08:30.046
there were people selling advertising,

00:08:30.046 --> 00:08:32.205
people opening restaurants,
people building businesses.

00:08:32.205 --> 00:08:33.754
Somebody's making money.

00:08:33.754 --> 00:08:36.523
So the excuse is bull, it's bull.

00:08:36.523 --> 00:08:39.539
So wake up in the morning
and own your failure.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:42.067
Look in the mirror and say
I'm failing because of me.

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:43.535
And you won't like it.

00:08:43.535 --> 00:08:44.920
And then you'll change it.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.245
But as long as you don't put it on you,

00:08:47.245 --> 00:08:49.282
you have no motivation to change it.

00:08:49.282 --> 00:08:52.135
So in short, if you own your failure,

00:08:52.135 --> 00:08:53.600
you'll own your success.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.331
If you don't own your
failure, you'll never dig out.

00:08:56.331 --> 00:08:58.328
And I find that in any business.

00:08:58.328 --> 00:09:00.814
Always the common denominator of failure,

00:09:00.814 --> 00:09:03.340
personally, is excuses.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.885
You don't want to be a failure do you ?

00:09:04.885 --> 00:09:05.900
- [Audience Member] Not at all.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.220
- You don't want to look in
the mirror and experience that.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.458
If you can't blame anybody but yourself,

00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:11.884
you're going to change.

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.961
You're going to fight
it out. That's the deal.

00:09:13.961 --> 00:09:15.306
- Failure is part of life.

00:09:15.306 --> 00:09:17.586
I mean, the difference for me though

00:09:17.586 --> 00:09:19.826
is I look at failure as a
stepping stone to success.

00:09:19.826 --> 00:09:22.717
It's a speed bump. I
know I'm going to fail.

00:09:22.717 --> 00:09:24.920
But it's not failure
if you learn something.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.611
And so, gosh, I've made so many mistakes,

00:09:27.611 --> 00:09:30.790
I've screwed so many things
up but every time I do,

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:33.685
it just becomes, it becomes
a way for me to explain

00:09:33.685 --> 00:09:35.193
to someone else what it takes.

00:09:35.193 --> 00:09:37.065
You know, it's like,
here's what I've done.

00:09:37.065 --> 00:09:39.142
I think I have the ability
to influence people

00:09:39.142 --> 00:09:40.609
because I talk about my failures.

00:09:40.609 --> 00:09:42.804
I talk about all the
things that mess me up.

00:09:42.804 --> 00:09:44.961
But I show people that I
didn't let them stop me

00:09:44.961 --> 00:09:46.513
and you don't let it stop you

00:09:46.513 --> 00:09:48.183
and I think that's
really the secret there.

00:09:48.183 --> 00:09:50.057
- Right and if everything
you touched was successful,

00:09:50.057 --> 00:09:51.808
you might not be able to
relate to people as much.

00:09:51.808 --> 00:09:52.828
- No you won't be able to relate

00:09:52.828 --> 00:09:54.294
and also, it's total bullshit.

00:09:54.294 --> 00:09:55.919
And everyone would know it's bullshit.

00:09:55.919 --> 00:09:57.424
And also, you'd be bored silly.

00:09:57.424 --> 00:09:58.644
I mean, think about it, if you just said

00:09:58.644 --> 00:10:00.922
I want this and it happened,
I want this and it happened,

00:10:00.922 --> 00:10:04.547
you know, people don't value
what they don't fight for.

00:10:04.547 --> 00:10:05.972
And it's like, you see kids sometimes

00:10:05.972 --> 00:10:07.399
and your parents will say,

00:10:07.399 --> 00:10:09.023
"You're not going to value
this if you don't work for it."

00:10:09.023 --> 00:10:10.083
and you're a kid going,

00:10:10.083 --> 00:10:12.123
"I'll value it, just give it to me."

00:10:12.123 --> 00:10:13.630
but it's true, you know?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.263
The things we work the
hardest for we value the most.

00:10:17.263 --> 00:10:19.502
So I think, you know,
the purpose of a goal

00:10:19.502 --> 00:10:20.642
is not getting it anyway,

00:10:20.642 --> 00:10:22.719
the purpose of a goal is who you become.

00:10:22.719 --> 00:10:24.750
Who you become is going
to make you happy or

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.078
it's going to make you sad.

00:10:26.078 --> 00:10:28.561
So, I'm not looking for
an effortless approach.

00:10:28.561 --> 00:10:30.046
There's no such thing.

